# Setup & Deployment Guide

## Why CSS Isn't Loading

The modular version (`index.html`) references external CSS with a relative path:
```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="css/styles.css" />
```

This fails when:
- ❌ Opening HTML directly with `file://` protocol
- ❌ Files aren't in correct directory structure
- ❌ Serving from GitHub Pages without proper folder setup
- ❌ Relative paths don't match file structure

---

## Solution 1: Use Standalone Version (EASIEST) ✅

**For GitHub Pages or quick testing:**

Use `index-standalone.html` instead — it has all CSS & JS embedded in a single file.

### Steps:
1. Rename `index-standalone.html` → `index.html` (replace the original)
2. Push to GitHub
3. It will work immediately on GitHub Pages

**Advantages:**
- Single file, no path issues
- Works everywhere (local, GitHub Pages, email)
- No setup required
- Easy to share

**Trade-off:**
- Not modular (harder to edit large codebases)
- Larger file size

---

## Solution 2: Fix Folder Structure (RECOMMENDED for Development)

Keep the modular setup but ensure proper structure:

### Required Structure:
```
your-repo/
├── index.html              ← Main file
├── css/
│   └── styles.css         ← Must be in css/ folder
├── js/
│   ├── data.js
│   ├── auth.js
│   ├── modal.js
│   ├── forms.js
│   ├── render.js
│   └── app.js
└── README.md
```

### Upload to GitHub:
```bash
# Initialize git
git init

# Add all files maintaining structure
git add .
git commit -m "Add Pulse Studio CRM"

# Push to GitHub
git remote add origin https://github.com/yourusername/pulse-studio-crm.git
git branch -M main
git push -u origin main
```

### Enable GitHub Pages:
1. Go to **Settings** → **Pages**
2. Select `main` branch as source
3. Save
4. Site will be available at `https://yourusername.github.io/pulse-studio-crm/`

### Run Locally:
```bash
# Python 3
python -m http.server 8000

# Python 2
python -m SimpleHTTPServer 8000

# Node.js
npx http-server

# Live Server (VS Code)
# Install "Live Server" extension, right-click index.html → "Open with Live Server"
```

**Advantages:**
- Modular, organized code
- Easy to maintain and update
- Industry standard structure
- Scalable for adding features

**Disadvantages:**
- Requires folder structure
- Must use web server (not `file://`)

---

## Solution 3: Inline CSS in index.html

If you want a single file but need modularity, add CSS to the `<head>`:

```html
<!doctype html>
<html>
<head>
  <style>
    /* All CSS here */
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <!-- HTML -->
  <script>
    // All JS here
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

